, divide it by 2 to get n / 2. If n is odd, multiply it by 3 and add 1 to obtain 3n + 1. Repeat the process (which has been called \"Half Or Triple Plus One\", or HOTPO) indefinitely. The conjecture is that no matter what number you start with, you will always eventually reach 1.","topics":["cpp14","mathematics","numbertheory"],"score":195456,"global_rank":325262},{"name":"michaelgokeefe/SimpleDraw_OpengGL","owner":"michaelgokeefe","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelgokeefe/SimpleDraw_OpengGL","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C++","description":"Learning OpenGL using c++ and freeglut. Tutorials/exercises taken from 3-D Computer Graphics - A Mathematical Introduction with OpenGL by Samuel R. Buss. ","topics":[],"score":195456,"global_rank":325294},{"name":"whu-tgsong/vscode_template","owner":"whu-tgsong","html_url":"https://github.com/whu-tgsong/vscode_template","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C++","description":"Template repo for working with vscode","topics":[],"score":195456,"global_rank":325305},{"name":"margretsteele/cppcon","owner":"margretsteele","html_url":"https://github.com/margretsteele/cppcon","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C++","description":"Notes from CPPCON 2016","topics":[],"score":195448,"global_rank":325354},{"name":"margretsteele/interview_problems","owner":"margretsteele","html_url":"https://github.com/margretsteele/interview_problems","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C++","description":"Interview problem solutions from CTCI","topics":[],"score":195448,"global_rank":325355},{"name":"annanay25/polly-precompiled","owner":"annanay25","html_url":"https://github.com/annanay25/polly-precompiled","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C++","description":"Precompiled Polly libraries for a temporary port to Bazel","topics":[],"score":195440,"global_rank":325387},{"name":"cdacamar/tiny_benchmark","owner":"cdacamar","html_url":"https://github.c